# P4b receipt: one pair, several relations, none of them ranked away.
#
# The claim is that the Related frontier stopped flattening. So this drives to a
# material whose neighbors are related more than one way, and asserts on the
# relation records themselves — how many, of which kinds, under which authority
# — rather than on a rendered string.
#
# Drive with testing/woodshed/run-scenario.ps1.

log P4b: typed relations, multiplicity retained
settle 3

# Chords, where the deterministic vocabulary is richest.
click .lens Chord
settle 3
assert snap lens == Chords

# The frontier holds pairs related several ways at once. The top row need not
# be one of them: an arpeggio realizes its chord and does only that, honestly.
assert snap related-multi-count >= 1
assert snap related-richest-relations >= 2
assert snap related-richest-kinds ~ shares tones
assert snap related-richest-kinds ~ voice-leads to
capture 01_related_multiplicity

# Every reason is deterministic here: no history has been recorded, so nothing
# in the frontier claims evidence it does not have.
assert snap related-richest-authorities ~ Computed
log authorities: deterministic only, before any practice is recorded

# Stage from the frontier: that records an engagement, which is what turns a
# later run's reasons into evidence-plus-theory rather than either alone.
click .related-stage
settle 3
assert snap set-cards == 1
capture 02_staged_from_frontier

log P4b receipt complete
